 "changed_since_previous": "No functional changes to the implementation; the commit was rebased or updated with an explanatory comment above the `CheckStatus()` call.",
 "card": "TxIndex::FindTx now checks the LevelDB iterator status after scanning candidates, throwing a dbwrapper_error if an underlying database failure or corruption occurred. Previously, iterator read failures caused the loop to terminate as if it had reached the end of the index, masking database errors as missing transactions. The author verified the issue by corrupting a test txindex database, showing that FindTx returned nullopt instead of raising an error. This follows up merged PR 35728, which addressed I/O error handling in GetTransaction.",
